# NASolve reviewed restraint dictionary DYI: O4-triazolyl-dU (supplier name),
# 4-(1,2,4-triazol-1-yl)-1-(2-deoxy-5-O-phosphono-beta-D-erythro-pentofuranosyl)pyrimidin-2(1H)-one.
# Not a wwPDB CCD component; DYI is a laboratory label. Parent DC (N4 = triazole N1).
# Built by scripts/build_dyi_dictionary.py from the CCP4 Monomer Library (AceDRG), commit 0af022bf6f7c401d59c7bf106e6709fc5f57c3d4:
#   d/DC.cif  blob f0373996ced17713c16643f30086bd5ad78a0628: all atoms shared with dC, unchanged
#   t/TZF.cif blob 6c477e8aa6a5d667efb18e8b6137a5e017a8c03f: triazol-1-yl ring, angles at N1, ring torsions and plane
# Chosen here: C4-N4 1.411 +/- 0.015 A (AceDRG 1.424 on C(C,C), 1.399 on C(N,N));
# N4 energy type NR5. Coordinates: DC's for shared atoms; triazole fitted, coplanar, N2T on the C5 side.
